{"at":"2026-10-13T11:18:41.625Z","tool":"open_session","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"questions\":\"1. **Which of the three proposed options ships?** The issue suggests a toggle in the panel, Ctrl+I / Cmd+I, or an italic font. Suggested: an \\\"Italic\\\" toggle in the properties panel next to the text align control (tooltip \\\"Italic (Ctrl+I)\\\"), plus the Ctrl+I / Cmd+I sho","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T11:19:06.203Z","tool":"record_answers","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"answers\":\"Answers from the product owner, relayed by the user. For questions these do not cover, the user accepted the suggested answer.\\n\\n1. (user) Italic ships as a panel toggle and Ctrl+I / Cmd+I. It is one italic property per text element, with no separate italic font. (accepted","outcome":"ok"}
